!! HTML element fallback

When the symbol after a glyph (with `allow-symbol: yes`) is a known HTML element name, the marker emits that element instead of the marker's default.

!!! Block aside

°aside.warn This becomes an `<aside>` element.

!!! Block section

°section.box This becomes a `<section>` element.

!!! Block summary inside details (note: standalone here, not nested)

°summary.bold Becomes a `<summary>` element.

!!! Inline em

This sentence has /°em emphasized text°/ which becomes an `<em>` element.

!!! Default when symbol is not an HTML name

°whatever Just the marker's default `<div>`, since `whatever` is not an HTML element.